Subject: fix(spec-review): count investigation.md as a reviewed input in the round-advance test

The round-advance gate refuses round N+1 unless requirements.md or
acceptance-tests.md changed since round N. But investigation.md is a
reviewed input too — it sits in every reviewer's allowed_input_manifest,
the calibration instructs reviewers to judge its Amendment Re-Review
Context section, and it has produced the blocking finding in five
consecutive rounds on epic-195-a7-compatibility. A remedy that lives
entirely in investigation.md therefore has NO permitted transition:
round N+1 is refused ("reviewed inputs are unchanged from the prior
round") and --reset is refused ("reset requires a terminal PASS or
BLOCKED contract") whenever the stalled round holds NEEDS_WORK. Both
refusals were reproduced verbatim today by an independent runner
(codex, attempt-8 open on epic-195), and the deadlock is the one
WFI-052 documents.

The fix completes the change-test's input set instead of loosening any
gate: round N+1 additionally opens when the live investigation.md hash
differs from the one the prior round's reviewer manifests pinned. A
round over byte-identical inputs is still refused; --reset semantics
are untouched; an attempt still cannot be abandoned mid-loop.

Apply from the repository root of the target worktree:

    git apply --check docs/ci-staging/round-advance-investigation.patch
    git apply docs/ci-staging/round-advance-investigation.patch

---
--- a/plugins/sdd-review-loop/scripts/spec-review-precheck.sh
+++ b/plugins/sdd-review-loop/scripts/spec-review-precheck.sh
@@ -343,7 +343,18 @@ if [[ "$round" -gt 1 ]]; then
   prior_requirements_sha="$(jq -r '.requirements_sha256' "$prior_contract")"
   prior_acceptance_sha="$(jq -r '.acceptance_sha256' "$prior_contract")"
-  [[ "$requirements_sha" != "$prior_requirements_sha" || "$acceptance_sha" != "$prior_acceptance_sha" ]] \
-    || fail "reviewed inputs are unchanged from the prior round"
+  # investigation.md is a reviewed input like the other two: it is pinned in
+  # every reviewer's manifest and the calibration instructs reviewers to judge
+  # its amendment record. A remedy confined to it must be able to open the
+  # next round, or the attempt deadlocks (WFI-052; reproduced on epic-195).
+  prior_investigation_sha="$(jq -r --arg p "specs/${feature}/investigation.md" '
+    [.reviewers[].allowed_input_manifest[]? | select(.path | endswith($p)) | .sha256] | first // empty
+  ' "$prior_contract")"
+  live_investigation_sha=""
+  [[ -f "${spec_dir}/investigation.md" ]] && live_investigation_sha="$(sha256 "${spec_dir}/investigation.md")"
+  investigation_changed=false
+  [[ -n "$prior_investigation_sha" && -n "$live_investigation_sha" && "$live_investigation_sha" != "$prior_investigation_sha" ]] && investigation_changed=true
+  [[ "$requirements_sha" != "$prior_requirements_sha" || "$acceptance_sha" != "$prior_acceptance_sha" || "$investigation_changed" == true ]] \
+    || fail "reviewed inputs are unchanged from the prior round"
 fi
 
 if [[ "$reset" == true ]]; then
--- a/plugins/sdd-review-loop/scripts/spec-review-precheck.ps1
+++ b/plugins/sdd-review-loop/scripts/spec-review-precheck.ps1
@@ -487,7 +487,20 @@ if ($roundInt -gt 1) {
   $priorData = Get-Content -LiteralPath $priorContract -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json
   $priorRequirementsSha = [string]$priorData.requirements_sha256
   $priorAcceptanceSha = [string]$priorData.acceptance_sha256
-  if ((Test-OrdinalEqual $requirementsSha $priorRequirementsSha) -and (Test-OrdinalEqual $acceptanceSha $priorAcceptanceSha)) {
+  # investigation.md is a reviewed input like the other two (WFI-052; see the
+  # sh twin's comment). A remedy confined to it must open the next round.
+  $priorInvestigationSha = ''
+  foreach ($reviewer in @($priorData.reviewers)) {
+    foreach ($entry in @($reviewer.allowed_input_manifest)) {
+      if ([string]$entry.path -like "*specs/$Feature/investigation.md") { $priorInvestigationSha = [string]$entry.sha256; break }
+    }
+    if ($priorInvestigationSha) { break }
+  }
+  $liveInvestigationPath = Join-Path $specDir 'investigation.md'
+  $liveInvestigationSha = ''
+  if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $liveInvestigationPath -PathType Leaf) { $liveInvestigationSha = (Get-FileHash -LiteralPath $liveInvestigationPath -Algorithm SHA256).Hash.ToLower() }
+  $investigationChanged = [bool]($priorInvestigationSha -and $liveInvestigationSha -and -not (Test-OrdinalEqual $liveInvestigationSha $priorInvestigationSha))
+  if ((Test-OrdinalEqual $requirementsSha $priorRequirementsSha) -and (Test-OrdinalEqual $acceptanceSha $priorAcceptanceSha) -and -not $investigationChanged) {
     Fail 'reviewed inputs are unchanged from the prior round'
   }
 }
 